WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.799
The Unreal Engine offers developers handy libraries that can be used during the development

2
00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:06.540
of their project.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.900
These libraries combine common functionality that we may want to use in multiple parts

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.099
of our projects, so let's take a quick look at some of the libraries we have available

5
00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:15.099
to us straight out of the box.

6
00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:19.359
As we said, Unreal offers a wide range of static classes to provide easily accessible

7
00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:23.480
and common functionality, such as lerping a value from A to B with a given alpha,

8
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.420
or a templated square value.

9
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.239
Some of these libraries are built in such a way that make them easy to expose the

10
00:00:29.239 --> 00:00:33.320
functionality out to blueprint, and this is commonly done through the use of the UBlueprint

11
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.640
function library class, alongside sensible UFunction macros.

12
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.359
As well as function libraries, developers are given access to the FMath static set

13
00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:46.820
of functions, which is a native only library that allows developers to make use of common

14
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:51.840
mathematical functions without needing to rewrite them from scratch.

15
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.579
These function libraries also give us access to gameplay functions that can be handy to

16
00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:56.579
use.

17
00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:00.100
For example, the Gameplay Statics library hosts a wide range of functions that allow

18
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.759
developers to spawn an actor from multiple sources, such as a blueprint pointer or a

19
00:01:03.759 --> 00:01:06.430
T subclass.

20
00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:09.370
Programmers can also leverage the blueprint function libraries to build their own set

21
00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.989
of static functions that can allow other developers on the project to make use of

22
00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:15.480
their own pieces of work.

23
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.060
By utilizing the reflection system, these functions can be made available to both programmers

24
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.739
in native and designers and artists in blueprint.
